{{History of Balisca}}

The '''right-wing insurgency in Balisca''', known in [[Anarchism in Balisca|anarchist]] literature as the '''Counter-Revolution''' ({{Langx|bl|Contrarrevolución}}), was a campaign of [[W:Rebellion|uprisings]] and [[W:Right-wing terrorism|terror attacks]] against the [[Revolutionary faction (Baliscan Revolution)|Baliscan Revolutionaries]] and their perceived supporters by oppositional [[W:Right-wing politics|right-wing organizations and groups]] that started soon after the [[Tragic Week]] and the formation of the [[Castejón Soviet]], continued through the years of the [[Processo Revolucionario en Curso|''Processo Revolucionario en Curso'']], and lasted up to the [[W:Great Depression|Great Depression]]. The insurgency was led or supported by right-wing groups such as the [[Triple A (Balisca)|Triple A]], [[Batallón Cerdanían]]'','' [[Warriors of Christ the King|Guerrilleros de Cristo Rey]] and [[Grupos Armados Balláran]].

The insurgency intensified in late 1919 as a result of the outcome of the [[1919 Confederal Convention|Confederal Convention]], and although the movement included a variety of political opinions in opposition to the revolution, the main force behind the movement were the dispossessed conservative economic and social elites (i.e. industrialists). As a result, the insurgency shared many traits with widespread right-wing counter-revolutionary movements of the time, namely [[W:Ultranationalism|ultranationalism]], [[W:Racism|racism]], [[W:Proto-fascism|proto-fascism]] and [[W:Criticism of democracy|opposition to democratic politics]], [[W:Clericalism|clericalism]] and contempt for the [[W:Working class|working class]]. The conservatives grew increasingly hard-line during the decisive and violent years following the Revolution, as expropriation/redistribution of wealth and other assets continued, [[W:Anti-clericalism|anti-clericalism]] intensified due to religious opposition to the revolution, and the new socialist regime was consolidated. These insurgent  attacks occurred mostly during a ten year period from 1919, until around 1930, though there did exist various small-scale attacks until Balisca's entry into the [[Great Adonian War]].

